 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 518851,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "$10,000 is deposited in an account bearing 5.6% interest for 5 years. Find the difference between the future value when the interest is simple interest and when the interest is compounded quarterly.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Future value with simple interest:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{\\rm{Future}}\\;{\\rm{Value}} = FV = P + I\"></span></p>\n<p>The interest <span data-math=\"(I)\"></span> is the principal <span data-math=\"(P)\"></span> times the annual simple interest rate as a decimal <span data-math=\"(r)\"></span> times the time in years <span data-math=\"(t)\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"I = P \\times r \\times t = 10,000 \\times 0.056 \\times 5 = \\$ 2,800\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"FV = P + I = 10,000 + 2,800 = \\$ 12,800\"></span></p>\n<p>Future value with compound interest:</p>\n<p>The future value of an investment, <span data-math=\"A\"></span>, when the principal, <span data-math=\"P\"></span>, is invested at an annual interest rate of <span data-math=\"r\"></span> (in decimal form), compounded <span data-math=\"n\"></span> times per year for <span data-math=\"t\"></span> years is found using the formula <span data-math=\"A = P{\\left({1 + \\frac{r}{n}} \\right)^{nt}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><i>Hint</i>: Find <span data-math=\"nt\"></span> before you plug numbers into your calculator! <span data-math=\"nt = \\left(4 \\right)\\left(5 \\right) = 20\"></span> It will help you get the right results. Use those parentheses in your calculator, too!</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = 10,000{\\left({1 + \\frac{{0.056}}{4}} \\right)^{20}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = \\$ 13,205.62\"></span></p>\n<p>The difference between the two methods: <span data-math=\"13205.62-12,800 = \\$ 405.62.\"></span></p>\n<p>You earn $405.62 more by compounding.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$405.62"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
